update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Typical business elements and examples are listed below. However, each organization can have unique value creation models and associated elements. | a) Value proposition: | b) Key activities: | c) Key business resources: | d) Customer segment: | e) Customer relationships: | f) Channels: | g) Costs: | h) Revenue streams: | i) Key partners: | j) Other elements: — printed p.5 to p.7', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §4.2 items a) to j), printed p.5-p.7 = PDF p.13-15, confirmed on the rendered pages. CAVEAT: the printed lead-in calls the list "typical" and says each organization "can have unique ... associated elements", so the 10-value enum closes a list the source leaves open, and the source treats a) to j) as a conjunction to be assessed, not a single pick - see STAGED R-6 [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='8e62c6da-5ec1-460e-b48e-eabe014e1fa8' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');


