-- ecosystem_regeneration_action
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='To align with the principle of ecosystem resilience, regeneration of degraded ecosystems can encompass removal of harmful substances and remediation of soil and water bodies, mitigation and adaptation to climate change impacts, and protection of biodiversity. These actions should ultimately lead to the conservation and continuous renewal of natural resources, improvements in water, soil and air quality, and prevention of land degradation. — printed p.16', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §4.6.5, printed p.16 = PDF p.24, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='d4a83518-0065-4050-9ff9-be135d32b831' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- transition_support_action
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='4.6.6 Actions to support a circular economy transition | 4.6.6.2 Education and research | 4.6.6.3 Innovation | 4.6.6.4 Collaboration and networks | 4.6.6.5 Helping users change their behaviour | 4.6.6.6 Policy and legal system | 4.6.6.7 Financial services | 4.6.6.8 Digitalization — printed p.16 to p.18', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §4.6.6 subclause headings, printed p.16-p.18 = PDF p.24-26, confirmed on the rendered pages; the 7 enum values reproduce the 7 printed headings exactly. §4.6.6.1 (printed p.16) adds: "Depending on the type of organizations, these actions can be considered as enablers." [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='22ff0fea-6e41-4f7d-9117-115143e29ad1' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- resource_management_action
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Table 2 - Guidance for resource management actions | Action / Description | Refuse: Make solutions redundant by abandoning its function or by offering the same function with a radically different solution. | Rethink | Source | Reduce | Repair | Re-use | Refurbish | Remanufacture | Repurpose | Cascade | Recycle | Recover energy | Re-mine: Mining or extraction from landfills and waste plants can be possible in some cases if mining or extraction activities are sustainably managed. — printed p.19', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - Table 2 (§4.6.7), printed p.19 = PDF p.27, table read off the rendered page; the 13 enum values reproduce the 13 printed Action rows in printed order exactly. OCR of this table was damaged ("radically different solutions", "stilin", "Adapta ... maior", "Recyele"); the printed page was used [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='895cb205-e9cd-498f-a264-7dfedda53705' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- life_cycle_perspective_applied
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='This resource management guidance is intended to help organizations prioritize actions to increase circularity performance. A life cycle perspective should guide the organization in the identification of the best action for their value creation model and to avoid unwanted trade-offs. | In general, products should be repaired before they are remanufactured, and remanufactured before they are recycled. However, in cases where applying this guidance does not lead to the best outcome, organizations should consider applying a life cycle perspective to determine the best action. — printed p.18 and p.19', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §4.6.7, printed p.18 = PDF p.26 (first passage) and printed p.19 = PDF p.27 (second passage), both confirmed on the rendered pages [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='1abc8c85-69b4-482b-9248-d05baf6b73d3' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');


-- ============================ WORKSHEET ISO-59010-06 - Strategie bestimmen ==================================

-- gaps_opportunities_identified
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Having assessed its current circularity performance or the value network within the defined boundary, as described in Clause 4, the organization should next identify the gaps and opportunities to transition its value creation model towards circularity. For this purpose, the elements of the value creation model (shown in the middle-left box of Figure 4) should be evaluated based on the circular economy principles defined in ISO 59004 (in the top box) to determine a circular economy strategy. — printed p.19', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §5.1, printed p.19 = PDF p.27, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='647b0e21-aa3c-44ab-b1b5-944b2c0403a4' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- circular_economy_principle
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The six circular economy principles (system thinking, value creation, value sharing, resource stewardship, resource traceability and ecosystem resilience) and their interconnection provide the basis for this strategy. | Figure 4 - Framework to determine a circular economy strategy, top box "Determining a strategy based on circular economy principles": Systems thinking / Value creation / Value sharing / Resource stewardship / Resource traceability / Ecosystem resilience — printed p.20', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §5.2 and Figure 4, printed p.20 = PDF p.28, both confirmed on the rendered page; the 6 enum values reproduce the 6 printed principles exactly. Two CAVEATS: (a) the body prints "system thinking" where Figure 4 prints "Systems thinking" - the encoding follows the figure; (b) the printed statement is a CONJUNCTION ("The six ... and their interconnection provide the basis"), while the field is a single-select - see STAGED R-6 [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='d50cae27-bbe3-4a97-a697-ddb0cee6644d' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- circular_economy_strategy
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='A strategy for the transition of an organization''s value creation model and value network to achieve the goals, i.e. a circular economy strategy, should be determined by considering the organization''s purpose, vision, mission, identified gaps and opportunities, its need to reposition within the value chain or the value network, its need to expand its sphere of influence and its desire to achieve a transition towards a more circular value creation model. — printed p.20', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §5.2, printed p.20 = PDF p.28, confirmed on the rendered page. §5.2 also prints: "The resulting circular economy strategy is on a case-by-case basis." (printed p.21) [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='0e84e7dc-be78-4fba-97c4-100766eaadc6' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- materiality_assessment_done
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Materiality is also a key consideration when developing a circular economy strategy. For example, many organizations conduct materiality assessments to assist in making decisions, especially when considering how to make their operations more sustainable. A common analysis method is to create a matrix with the vertical axis representing interested parties'' expectations for the organization and the horizontal axis representing the organization''s business priorities. — printed p.21', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §5.2, printed p.21 = PDF p.29, confirmed on the rendered page. "materiality" and "materiality assessment" are defined at §3.8 and §3.9. Correctly is_required=false: the printed modality is "many organizations conduct" [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='c9f3e72b-fba4-44fd-9cae-7ab726bf6af8' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- economic_rationalization_done
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Irrespective of the interested parties'' expectations or the organization''s desire to shift to a circular value creation model, the actual transition cannot successfully be conducted without economic rationalization. All value creation models presume an ability to realize a profit while taking into account the associated risks. — printed p.21', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §5.3, printed p.21 = PDF p.29, confirmed on the rendered page. This is the strongest statement in the document; it is still not a "shall" [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='6cff7fff-6586-42e8-b6ae-5fc1b47d9ef9' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');


-- ============================ WORKSHEET ISO-59010-07 - Wertschoepfungsmodell umstellen ======================

-- transition_plan
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='After a circular economy strategy is set, the next step is to develop a transition plan to shift from the current to the desired future. | An organization''s transition plan should include objectives, timelines, actions and anticipated interim results. — printed p.22', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §6.1, printed p.22 = PDF p.30, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='5982a448-d791-452b-8458-3517a20e35d1' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- plan_objectives_in_kpis
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The objectives and interim results should be expressed in KPIs used to assess the status of circularity as described in 4.6. The plan should be in line with the circular economy strategy as described in 5.2. — printed p.22', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §6.1, printed p.22 = PDF p.30, confirmed on the rendered page. SOURCE INCONSISTENCY (the document''s own, not the encoding''s): §6.1 and §7.2 point to 4.6 for these KPIs while §8.1 points to 4.5; the KPI selection clause is 4.5 - see STAGED R-11 [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='20698e1e-344b-4aa7-b45d-52606d8ce566' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- value_model_element_reviewed
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The organization should consider changes to its value creation model that are consistent with the developed plan. Examples of such considerations are given in 6.2.2 to 6.2.11. — printed p.22', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §6.2.1, printed p.22 = PDF p.30, confirmed on the rendered page. CAVEAT: the printed text calls 6.2.2-6.2.11 "Examples of such considerations" [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='3abade2e-151b-4498-bda3-cc326195479b' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- value_proposition_reviewed
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='A value proposition for circularity includes how the target group''s needs can be fulfilled while keeping resources at their highest value for as long as possible. This can be done by considering a product''s lifetime over several use cycles in which the maximum value is created by cascading materials through circular actions such as reuse, repair, remanufacturing and recycling. — printed p.22', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §6.2.2, printed p.22 = PDF p.30, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='1fbd291b-f5b3-48fb-89bf-566a93122e88' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- recovered_resources_prioritized
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='As a key business resource in a circular value creation model, recovered resources obtained via, for example, reusing or recycling products, parts or materials take precedence over virgin resources extracted from the earth. — printed p.22', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §6.2.4, printed p.22 = PDF p.30, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='18f18c4b-b38c-45c8-a5ab-be63eb7954b3' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- other_consideration
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='In addition to the considerations listed in 6.2.2 to 6.2.11, an organization can identify potential risks and opportunities by exploring: | current/future compliance obligations; | current solutions that are related to end-to-end processes (life cycle perspective); | market and societal perspectives of linear value networks; | potential unintended consequences from implementing circular economy solutions; | use of renewable energy; | education and awareness of circular economy objectives. — printed p.24', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §6.2.12, printed p.24 = PDF p.32, confirmed on the rendered page; the 6 enum values reproduce the 6 printed dashes exactly [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='d2181237-daf4-4b9f-89b8-0d4e69a2dd31' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');


-- ============================ WORKSHEET ISO-59010-08 - Wertschoepfungsnetzwerk umstellen ====================

-- boundary_expanded
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='In many cases, during the transition to circularity, it is necessary to expand the project''s boundary to include a broader perspective beyond the organization''s immediate value chain. Expanding the boundary of the existing value chain beyond solely commercial relationships can create opportunities to develop circular flows of resources by regenerating ecosystems, and retaining or adding to their value. — printed p.24', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.1, printed p.24 = PDF p.32, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='73111e4c-2c5f-4c5a-b6c5-b7eee158db1c' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- shared_objectives_defined
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Value network members should determine their shared objectives by considering potential symbiotic opportunities and members'' individual circular objectives. — printed p.25', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.2 (opening), printed p.25 = PDF p.33, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='b407c511-02fa-4a6d-930f-9b47c3fabc61' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- shared_strategy_plan
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The members can decide to create a shared circular economy strategy based on those shared objectives in addition to each member''s circular economy strategy. | Value network members should break down the shared objectives into actions and create a shared plan with timelines with expected interim results and associated actions to shift their value networks towards circularity. — printed p.25', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.2, printed p.25 = PDF p.33, confirmed on the rendered page. CAVEAT: the SHARED STRATEGY half is printed as "can decide", only the SHARED PLAN half is a "should"; the field is is_required=true for both - see STAGED R-5 [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='808e1c49-47af-4262-aebb-8e3ddd910810' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- consistency_verification_done
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Participating members of the value network should engage in consistency verification to ensure alignment in objectives, values, governance and decision-making throughout the network. Open communication between the members can be instrumental in resolving any potential misalignments. — printed p.26', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.2, printed p.26 = PDF p.34, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='13e3aca8-f702-43ce-997a-0baee44ff383' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- governance_structure
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='A governance structure should be implemented in a value network. Depending on the network objectives and strategy, the governance structures can take diverse forms. | EXAMPLE A forum, an alliance, pacts, a consortium, members networks, public-private partnerships. — printed p.26', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.3, printed p.26 = PDF p.34, confirmed on the rendered page. "governance" is defined at §3.5 (printed p.2) as "principles, policies and framework by which an organization is directed and controlled" [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='8a776108-7358-492c-a2f5-ca979b3886a5' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- governance_element
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The following elements should be considered for governance: | clear roles and responsibilities of members; | principle of respect for the liberty and free will of each member; | establishing an advisory group, steering committee or governing board; | shared by-laws that provide the principles and rules by which shared objectives and strategies are to be achieved; | clear and active communication channels and protocols between members and external interested parties; | risk management (member impartiality and inclusivity); | fostering of trust-building and engagement; | transparent decision-making processes; | traceability mechanisms; | reporting processes to interested parties, community and key partners, especially non-financial disclosure. — printed p.26', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.3, printed p.26 = PDF p.34, confirmed on the rendered page; the 10 enum values reproduce the 10 printed dashes exactly. CAVEAT: the printed lead-in is a conjunction ("The following elements should be considered"), while the field is a single-select - see STAGED R-6 [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='fbbf9b4e-f676-44df-aa65-7f4ccdac416a' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- shared_infrastructure
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Collaboration between members in a circular value network often requires shared infrastructure, sometimes provided by value network members. Example components of such an infrastructure include: | an information exchange platform for participating parties and their external interested parties (e.g. block-chain, digital material, product passports); | shared facilities and assets that achieve shared objectives such as (reverse) logistics, warehouses, treatment of PCM, land and energy recovery; | leveraged knowledge and skills to deploy relevant technologies and social and capital innovations. — printed p.26', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §7.4, printed p.26 = PDF p.34, confirmed on the rendered page; the 3 enum values reproduce the 3 printed dashes exactly. CAVEAT: the printed lead-in says "Example components ... include", so the enum closes an explicitly exemplary list; gate CR-019 nevertheless tests it IS NOT NULL - see STAGED R-7 [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='4b9a482c-14c3-476c-ac4f-0ad6eb227862' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');


-- ============================ WORKSHEET ISO-59010-09 - Pruefung & Ueberwachung ==============================

-- performance_measured
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='After selecting actions to improve circularity, an organization should measure and assess the results of those actions as its circularity performance, which aligns with the KPIs described in 4.5. — printed p.26', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §8.1 (opening), printed p.26 = PDF p.34, confirmed on the rendered page [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='88291662-09d2-46ad-92e3-dc2105cead90' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- measurement_meaningful
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='Measurement and assessment of circularity performance should be meaningful, i.e. the data needs to be relevant and precise enough for the intended application. Data acquisition should be organized across value chains or value networks, with regard to the amount of data and its quality. | The measurement should include all resource inflows and outflows (including emissions and losses) by applying the core circularity indicators of ISO 59020. — printed p.27', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §8.1, printed p.27 = PDF p.35, confirmed on the rendered page. NR CAVEAT: the core circularity indicators live in ISO 59020, a separate document [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='e0ec4881-5da4-4601-b192-68c59fd656e1' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- complementary_method
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The assessment of impacts on social, environmental and economic aspects is part of the assessment step as explained in ISO 59020. It can be made by applying complementary methods (e.g. ISO 14044 for LCA, ISO 26000 for social responsibility). — printed p.27', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §8.1, printed p.27 = PDF p.35, confirmed on the rendered page. Correctly is_required=false: the printed modality is "can be made" and the two standards are "e.g." [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='58994603-9d3a-4521-818c-d8db8973a983' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- periodic_assessment
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='The outcome of the measurement and assessment process is specific to a defined time period for which the measurement and assessment are conducted. To monitor progress over time, the organization can choose to carry out periodic assessments. — printed p.27', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §8.1, printed p.27 = PDF p.35, confirmed on the rendered page. The document names NO interval, frequency or period length anywhere - correctly is_required=false and correctly unquantified in prod [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='6767b276-55be-4cc2-87b7-220333ad23c4' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- value_model_improvement_reviewed
update public.fields set verification_status='verified_against_standard', verification_quote='At an appropriate interval, such as when interim results are achieved, the plan as described in 6.1 should be reviewed from, but not limited to, the following perspectives: | a) Achieved performance: the interim results described in 6.1 should be checked, and improvement opportunities identified if results are not on target to achieve goals. | b) Value creation model elements: The value creation model elements investigated in 4.2 and 6.2 should be reviewed for further continuous improvement opportunities. | c) Access to finance and funding — printed p.27', verification_note='md-verified 2026-09-09 - source: ISO/FDIS 59010:2024(en), FINAL DRAFT International Standard (a ballot draft, NOT the published ISO 59010) - §8.2, printed p.27 = PDF p.35, confirmed on the rendered page. The printed interval is "At an appropriate interval, such as when interim results are achieved" - no number is printed and none is encoded [VA-OCR]', verified_at=now() where id='4232be61-4324-4ad6-aef2-a822c6025473' and verification_status not in ('verified_against_standard','corrected');

-- value_network_improvement_reviewed
